# Architecture

Local code-change board (not deployments/runtime ops). Talks to GitHub, GitLab and Azure DevOps through their CLIs on the machine, and to Bitbucket through its REST API.

| Layer | Choice |
|-------|--------|
| GitHub | `gh` |
| GitLab | `glab` |
| Azure DevOps | `az devops` / `az repos` / `az pipelines` |
| Bitbucket | Bitbucket Cloud REST API over `net/http` (no curl); credentials from the environment (`BITBUCKET_TOKEN`, or `BITBUCKET_USERNAME` + `BITBUCKET_APP_PASSWORD`) |
| Auth | Existing CLI login sessions; Bitbucket env credentials |
| Tracing | [olly](https://github.com/behaviorengineering/olly) `olly.Init` + `pkg/dump` failure dumps, set up in `serve` and `sync` |
| AI triage | Optional OpenAI-compatible chat in config `llm` |
| Agent sessions | `strop/agentsession` (prune investigate) via published module |
| Supervision | process-compose (`go tool task serve`); `gitboard serve` for one-off |

## Packages

`pkg/` is a public library for other Go modules: its exported API never takes or
returns an `internal/` type, and every `pkg/` package comment says it is public API.
`internal/` holds the binary's wiring and is grouped by domain.

```
cmd/gitboard/                # entrypoint: version stamp, signals, cli.Execute
pkg/board/                   # JSON DTOs for the dashboard UI and forge adapters (PruneHint, AppearanceRole)
pkg/boardconfig/             # config document types and pure rules (File, Project, Host, View, Normalize)
pkg/clock/                   # Clock: the one injected time source for stamps and TTLs
pkg/gberr/                   # domain error: Code, Op, client-safe Msg, Fields, Cause
pkg/cliexec/                 # shared gh/glab/az/git exec (re-exports gitvalet gitexec)
pkg/remotegit/               # forge adapters (GitHub, GitLab, Azure DevOps, Bitbucket) + TTLCache
pkg/remotegit/remotegittest/ # test-only fake Exec and forge fixtures (conformity, benchmarks)
pkg/localgit/                # checkouts and worktrees: read-only Inspector, lease-bound Mutator
pkg/projectsync/             # forge discovery from sync sources + tracked-set selection rules
pkg/dashboard/               # Service (read) and Commands (write); ServiceConfig.CreateService
internal/cli/                # Cobra command tree: init, sync, serve, version, agent guide
internal/cli/syncprompt/     # interactive sync terminal UI (candidate list, prompts)
internal/config/             # config file discovery, YAML load/save, init, env overlays
internal/server/             # HTTP + static UI
internal/server/static/      # dashboard assets
internal/server/timing/      # Server-Timing header recorder
internal/ai/llm/             # OpenAI-compatible client
internal/ai/triage/          # AI failure triage
internal/ai/pruneagent/      # investigate removable branches
internal/observability/      # injected Logger (tracing and dumps come from olly)
internal/testing/conformity/ # network retrieval contracts across upstreams
internal/testing/benchnet/   # call-count and latency benchmarks
```

**Dependency direction:** `cmd` → `internal/*` and `pkg/*`; `internal/*` may import `pkg/*`; `pkg/*` never imports `internal/*`; domain packages must not import `cmd`. Prefer `cliexec` for process calls. Keep `main` to wiring; Cobra `RunE` handlers in `internal/cli` parse flags and call services. `internal/cli/wiring.go` builds the shared runner and `dashboard.ServiceConfig` for `serve` and `sync`.

**Local git writes:** `localgit.Inspector` only reads. Fetch, pull, safe prune and index.lock clearing exist only on `localgit.Mutator`, obtained from a held `MutationLease` (`lease.Mutator(run)`); each method refuses a path whose common git dir is not the leased one. `dashboard.LocalGit` mirrors this (`LocalScanner`, `LocalComparer`, `Mutator(lease) LocalMutator`). The prune agent shares the dashboard's `MutationCoordinator`.

**Errors:** every service returns `*gberr.Error` (`gberr.New`, `gberr.Wrap`, `.With(k, v)`). `Msg` is client-safe; `Cause` and `Fields` (paths, CLI stderr, argv) are for logs only. `gberr.CodeOf` reads the outermost code (a bare context error is `CodeCanceled`, anything untyped is `CodeInternal`). The server maps codes in one place, `internal/server/errors.go`: Invalid 400, NotFound 404, Conflict 409, ConfirmRequired 409 (with the `dashboard.ConfirmRequiredError` JSON), Canceled 504, Unavailable 503, Internal 500 (never sends `Msg`). `writeError` logs the chain with `op`, `code` and fields and sets `X-Gitboard-Error-Code`. The CLI maps the same codes to exit codes (`internal/cli/exit.go`): 0 ok, 1 internal, 2 invalid or usage, 3 conflict, 4 not found, 5 unavailable, 6 cancelled. Forge adapters return CodeUnavailable for forge failures (Canceled on cancel, Invalid for a bad path, run or job id); `remotegit.forgeErr` and `repoPathErr` build them. Display text in `summary.Error`, `local.error` and `Evidence.Notes` still carries forge and git detail.

**Prune rules:** one pure function, `dashboard.pruneVerdict(PruneInputs) PruneVerdict{Allow, Hint, Candidate, Reason}` in `pkg/dashboard/prune_verdict.go`, decides every prune hint and every `PruneSafe` refusal. It refuses when remote names or open reviews did not load (`ProjectSummary.RemoteNamesOK`, `OpenOK`), when the default branch is unknown, when a merged lookup failed, and when the branch is the default, still on the forge, or has an open review. `PruneSafe` re-runs it on the unfiltered forge branches and only then takes the lease.

**Origin sync:** `localgit.Inspector.OriginSync(ctx, dir) (RepoSync, error)` runs one `git for-each-ref` per common git dir (track counts plus `%(ahead-behind:origin/HEAD)` on git 2.41 and newer) and `RepoSync.Apply` copies it to each worktree; only branches whose upstream is not `origin/<same name>` run `rev-list`. Fetches go through `Mutator.FetchOriginSmart(ctx, repo, FetchPolicy{TTL, Fresh, Branches}, cache)`. `localgit.Discovery.Warnings` lists skipped roots and checkouts; the dashboard sends them as `local_warnings`.

**Time:** every stamp and TTL reads one `clock.Clock` set at the entrypoint (`dashboard.ServiceConfig.Clock`, `pruneagent.Config.Clock`); `remotegit.NewTTLCache`, `localgit.NewOriginFetchCache` and `remotegit.SummaryOpts.Now` require it. Durations (`time.Since`) stay on the wall clock.

**Budgets:** deadlines are set once at the entrypoint: per-route budgets in `internal/server/server.go`, `syncBudget` and `cliCallBudget` in `internal/cli`. Leaves fail closed without a deadline (`cliexec.ErrMissingDeadline`, the Bitbucket transport, `llm.Chat`) and add none of their own; the per-project forge budget is `dashboard.CollectOpts.RowBudget`, set by the HTTP handler.

**Config:** `pkg/boardconfig` holds the document types and rules (`File.Normalize`, `ParseHost`, `SplitRepoPath`, TTL getters); `internal/config` only finds, loads and saves the file and applies env overlays. `pkg/projectsync` discovers candidates and applies a selection; `gitboard sync` and the Manage API both go through `dashboard.Commands` (`SetSyncSources`, `ApplySelection`, `ApplySyncSelection`, `AddTrackedProject`, `RemoveTrackedProject`).

**Observability:** `serve` and `sync` call `olly.Init` once (`internal/cli/observe.go`). The OTLP endpoint is `GITBOARD_OPENINFERENCE_ENDPOINT`, `POLYPUS_OTLP_ENDPOINT` or `openinference.endpoint`, then olly's `OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_*` fallback. The server wraps `/api/` in an olly SERVER span per request; a request that ends 5xx writes a failure dump (`<trace id>.json`) under `openinference.failure_dump.dir` when dumps are on (`serve` only). `sync` runs under one command span. The LLM client sends through `ollyhttp.Client`. Git and forge CLI hops get client spans from gitvalet once its olly release is pinned.

**API guard:** every `/api/` request passes `apiGuard` (`internal/server/guard.go`): the `Host` header must be a name of this server (loopback names on the bound port, plus the host name and interface addresses on a wildcard bind), which stops DNS rebinding on reads too. Any method other than GET or HEAD must also have a same-site `Origin` (or none) and `Content-Type: application/json`. With `serve --allow-non-localhost`, a random per-launch token is printed once at startup and required in `X-Gitboard-Token` on every write; the UI reads it from same-origin `GET /api/meta`. The UI sends every write through `mutationHeaders()` in `static/app.js`.

## strop dependency

`go.mod` requires the published module (`github.com/behaviorengineering/strop vX.Y.Z`). No git submodule.

**Bump a release:** `go get github.com/behaviorengineering/strop@vX.Y.Z` then `go mod tidy`.

**Local strop changes (rare):** develop in a sibling clone, temporarily add it to root `go.work`, then release strop and bump the require. Do not commit a long-lived `replace` or re-add a submodule unless the user asks.

```
# sibling layout example
use (
	.
	../strop
)
```

After the strop PR/tag lands: remove the sibling `use` line (keep `go.work` with `.` only), `go get …@vX.Y.Z`, `go mod tidy`.

## Dashboard behavior

- Project list order (UI): attention first (failed CI, conflicts, open review, dirty, prune hint, behind-only vs origin on a real pull candidate), then A–Z by label. Behind attention matches the pull affordance: detached pins (common for submodules) and their unrelated `origin_sync` branch rows do not count. Active search keeps relevance first, then the same attention / A–Z tiebreak. Config `projects` order is not the board order.
- **Views:** config `views` are named subsets of tracked project ids (membership may overlap). `GET /api/dashboard?view=<id>` forge-loads only that subset. Empty/omitted `views` synthesizes an implicit `default` view over all projects. The UI switcher persists the active view in localStorage. Switching a view selects the tab immediately, shows a busy spinner on that tab while the fetch runs (dimmer fill while loading, brighter active fill when done), paints a per-view cache instantly when available, then refreshes in the background. First load and uncached view switches use `?stream=1` (NDJSON shell stubs then per-project fill-in); quiet polls and cache-hit refreshes stay on one-shot JSON. There is no “load everything” control in v1.
- Branches column: remote heads from the forge (up to 20); default + open PR/MR first, then by recency. Each row has its own latest CI. CI-only refs do not invent branch rows. Empty `ui.hide_branches` shows all; `path.Match` patterns hide matching names from the board only (forge prune data unchanged), including UI “local only” rows synthesized from local checkouts. After hide, `open_items` and the Open review chip / attention rank count only still-visible `open_review` branches.
- Local status beside each remote branch (checked out, dirty, ↑/↓ vs origin). Ahead/behind uses origin refresh (TTL: `local.fetch_seconds`, default 120; `?fresh=1` bypasses) then compares local heads to `origin/<branch>`. Warm polls use a targeted `git fetch origin <branch>…` for visible forge branches plus local heads; full TTL expiry or `fresh=1` uses `git fetch --prune origin` (targeted fetches do not prune). Behind + clean → **pull** is ff-only (`git pull --ff-only`, or `git fetch origin branch:branch` when not checked out), then `git submodule update --init --recursive` on the checked-out worktree so nested submodule pins match the new tip. Stale submodule checkouts that only look dirty are synced before pull refuses a dirty tree. Each local appearance (checkout/submodule) with behind-only + clean also gets its own pull control; pulls start immediately (no confirm) and may run in parallel. If `index.lock` is older than 30s, pull and safe-remove return HTTP 409 `stale_index_lock` so the UI can ask to remove the lock and retry with `clear_index_lock`; a fresher lock is refused (another git process may still be running). **Prune hints** (remote head gone + clean + no open PR/MR): **safe** when the forge has a merged PR/MR for that branch name (recent merged list or a per-branch lookup), or local tip content already matches default (`origin/<default>` preferred; ancestor or identical trees, covering squash merges). **likely** only after a per-branch merged lookup confirms there is no matching PR/MR; a missing page of recent merges is not enough. Missing forge data shows no hint. A branch still listed in the UI Branches column (or with an open review) never gets a prune hint, even if content-on-default would otherwise say safe. Investigate uses the same content-on-default check so unique SHAs alone do not force keep after squash. **Safe prune** on the main worktree updates the default branch from origin before switching onto it and deleting the merged branch (ff-only when possible; if default is not checked out and has diverged, the local default tip is moved to `origin/<default>`, discarding local-only commits on that tip). Worktrees with no remote head are “local only”. Detached HEAD that matches a tag exactly shows the tag name (SHA in tooltip), not only `detached <sha>`. Submodule worktree paths resolve to the checkout (`git rev-parse --show-toplevel`), not the `.git/modules` git dir.
- Failed CI: project payload `capabilities.failed_jobs` is true for GitHub and GitLab (failed-job list + AI triage control). Azure DevOps and Bitbucket adapters exist for config/API and tracked projects, but the UI does not surface them yet (tooling strip, Manage Sources, Discover, and the interactive `gitboard sync` prompt stay GitHub + GitLab only).
- `gitboard sync` and the board **Manage** UI write config; a running `serve` reloads the full config file when its mtime advances and clears the forge + origin-fetch TTL caches when the tracked project set, view membership, or `local.roots` changes (no restart required for add/remove, views, roots, or `ui.hide_branches` edits). Manage **Tracked** lists projects under host subtabs (GitHub, GitLab, …) sorted A–Z by label within the active host; **Discover**, **Views**, **Local**, and **Sources** cover the rest of sync config (Sources and Discover advertise GitHub + GitLab only).

## HTTP API

| Method | Path | Purpose |
|--------|------|---------|
| `GET` | `/api/health` | Liveness |
| `GET` | `/api/meta` | Server meta (`poll_interval_seconds`, `ui.hide_branches`, `views`, `tooling`, and `token` when the server has one) |
| `GET` | `/api/dashboard` | Aggregated rows for one view (`?view=` required for non-default; `?fresh=1` forces refresh; `?stream=1` NDJSON: shell → project* → done or error); includes `ui`, `views`, `active_view`, `local_warnings` |
| `GET` | `/api/failures?project=&run_id=` | Failed jobs |
| `POST` | `/api/triage` | AI log analysis |
| `POST` | `/api/prune/safe` | Re-check hints; remove a safe local checkout (`clear_index_lock` after 409 `stale_index_lock`) |
| `POST` | `/api/pull/ff` | Fast-forward local branch from origin (ff-only; same `clear_index_lock` confirm) |
| `POST` | `/api/local/sync/investigate` | Refresh origin and compare local branch commits |
| `POST` | `/api/agents/prune/investigate` | Likely-removable branch evidence + session card |
| `GET` | `/api/agents/sessions/:id` | Session meta, card, turns |
| `GET` | `/api/agents/sessions/:id/failure` | Failure dump when present |
| `GET` | `/api/sync/candidates` | Discover forge repos from `sync` sources (`?host=`); JSON `candidates` plus optional `warnings` for per-source forge failures |
| `POST` | `/api/sync/projects` | Add, remove, or set `local_path` on a tracked project (`action` add/remove/set_local_path) |
| `PUT` | `/api/sync/selection` | Replace tracked set from selected host/path refs |
| `GET`/`PUT` | `/api/sync/sources` | Read/update GitHub orgs, GitLab groups, Azure DevOps orgs, and Bitbucket workspaces |
| `GET`/`PUT` | `/api/local/roots` | Read/update `local.roots` scan directories |
| `GET`/`PUT` | `/api/views` | Read sync state / replace named view definitions |

Response bodies are typed structs in `internal/server/responses.go`. Every config write (`/api/sync/projects`, `/api/sync/selection`, the PUTs) runs one flow, `configWrite[B].handler`: guards, decode, apply through `dashboard.Commands`, save, reload, render from the reloaded file.

